<!-- BOOKS -->
<section id="books">
  <div class="books-layout">
    <div class="books-quote">
      <p class="section-label">My Bookshelf</p>
      <blockquote>
        "A reader lives a thousand lives before he dies. The man who never reads lives only one."
      </blockquote>
      <cite>— George R.R. Martin</cite>
      <p style="font-size:0.85rem; color: var(--text-light); margin-top:1.2rem; line-height:1.7; font-weight:300;">
        I have a special love for authors from South and Southeast Asia — voices that carry a personal resonance, stories rooted in the soil I know.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Books Close to My Heart</h2>
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <div class="booklist">
        <div class="book-item">
          <div class="book-spine" style="background: var(--deep-green);"></div>
          <div class="book-info">
            <h4>Clear Light of Day & In Custody</h4>
            <p class="book-author">Anita Desai</p>
            <p class="book-note">Desai's writing is quietly devastating — she captures the inner worlds of women and families in India with extraordinary sensitivity and depth. Her prose feels like a meditation.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="book-item">
          <div class="book-spine" style="background: var(--earth);"></div>
          <div class="book-info">
            <h4>The Namesake & Interpreter of Maladies</h4>
            <p class="book-author">Jhumpa Lahiri</p>
            <p class="book-note">Lahiri writes about identity, belonging and the immigrant heart with such tenderness. Her stories resonate deeply — especially for anyone who has lived between cultures and continents.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="book-item">
          <div class="book-spine" style="background: var(--sage);"></div>
          <div class="book-info">
            <h4>The Palace of Illusions & Sister of My Heart</h4>
            <p class="book-author">Chitra Banerjee Divakaruni</p>
            <p class="book-note">Divakaruni weaves mythology, womanhood and South Asian experience into stories that are utterly captivating. The Palace of Illusions gave Draupadi a voice I never forgot.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="book-item">
          <div class="book-spine" style="background: var(--bark);"></div>
          <div class="book-info">
            <h4>Voices from South & Southeast Asia</h4>
            <p class="book-author">Various Authors</p>
            <p class="book-note">I am drawn to writers from this part of the world — there is a personal connect in their stories, a familiar warmth, a truth that feels close to home.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- MUSIC -->
<section id="music">
  <div class="music-layout">
    <div class="music-text">
      <p class="section-label">Music & Soul</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">My Lifelong Companion</h2>
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <p>Music has always been the thread running through the fabric of my life. I grew up with the golden era of the 80s and 90s — a time when music had soul, lyrics had meaning, and every song told a story worth hearing.</p>
      <p>My heart belongs especially to <strong>Dire Straits</strong> — Mark Knopfler's guitar is something I will never tire of. There is a certain magic in that sound — soulful, unhurried, deeply human. Music like that doesn't age; it only deepens.</p>
