<!-- LEARNING -->
<section id="learning" style="background: var(--forest); padding: 6rem; color: white;">
  <p class="section-label" style="color:var(--sage);">Always a Student</p>
  <h2 class="section-title" style="color:var(--warm-sand);">The Joy of Learning — What Keeps Me Going</h2>
  <div class="divider" style="background:var(--earth);"></div>

  <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 4rem; align-items: start;">
    <div>
      <p style="font-size:1.05rem; font-weight:300; line-height:1.9; color:rgba(255,255,255,0.75); margin-bottom:1.2rem;">
        Learning is the thread that runs through everything I do. It is not something I do out of obligation — it is something I do out of <strong style="color:white;">pure joy</strong>. The moment I stop learning, I stop growing. And growing, for me, is simply being alive.
      </p>
      <p style="font-size:1.05rem; font-weight:300; line-height:1.9; color:rgba(255,255,255,0.75); margin-bottom:1.2rem;">
        I have recently discovered the exciting world of <strong style="color:white;">Artificial Intelligence</strong> — and especially <strong style="color:white;">Claude</strong>! The possibilities feel endless, and every conversation, every experiment, every new tool opens up a new horizon. Whether it is creating an Instagram carousel or exploring what AI can do for education — I am all in.
      </p>
      <p style="font-size:1.05rem; font-weight:300; line-height:1.9; color:rgba(255,255,255,0.75);">
        I have completed several courses from <strong style="color:white;">Harvard University</strong> — in leadership, in education, in the craft of leading people and institutions. The title may say CEO — Principal, but in my heart, I will always be a student first. That joy of learning? It keeps me going, every single day. ✨
      </p>
    </div>

